3. Analytical SQL Queries (30)
Run the schema and sample-data scripts first, then execute these queries in PostgreSQL. The queries use PostgreSQL syntax such as
FILTER, ILIKE, and NULLS LAST.
1. View all student records
Display all student profiles.
SELECT * FROM students ORDER BY student_id;
2. List students by branch
Show students sorted by branch and name.
SELECT student_id, student_name, branch, cgpa
FROM students
ORDER BY branch, student_name;
3. Students with CGPA 8 or above
Find students meeting a CGPA threshold.
SELECT student_id, student_name, branch, cgpa
FROM students
WHERE cgpa >= 8.00
ORDER BY cgpa DESC;
4. Count students by branch
Count student records in each branch.
SELECT branch, COUNT(*) AS total_students
FROM students
GROUP BY branch
ORDER BY total_students DESC;
5. Average CGPA by branch
Calculate average academic performance by branch.
SELECT branch, ROUND(AVG(cgpa), 2) AS average_cgpa
FROM students
GROUP BY branch
ORDER BY average_cgpa DESC;
6. Highest and lowest CGPA by branch
Compare the CGPA range across branches.
SELECT branch, MAX(cgpa) AS highest_cgpa, MIN(cgpa) AS lowest_cgpa
FROM students
GROUP BY branch;
7. Branch-wise placement rate
Count distinct students with at least one successful placement.
SELECT s.branch,
COUNT(*) AS total_students,
COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE EXISTS (
SELECT 1 FROM placements p
WHERE p.student_id = s.student_id AND p.placement_status = 'Placed'
)) AS placed_students,
ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE EXISTS (
SELECT 1 FROM placements p
WHERE p.student_id = s.student_id AND p.placement_status = 'Placed'
)) / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0), 2) AS placement_percentage
FROM students s
GROUP BY s.branch
ORDER BY placement_percentage DESC;
